        F: 'From the odd 2p⁵ ²P° ground state the two-photon intermediates must be odd as well: the 2p⁴3p levels at 116,987–117,873 cm⁻¹, which need 2 × 171–170 nm, below any doubled-dye output. The even 2p⁴3s ⁴P and ²P levels at 102,406–105,056 cm⁻¹ are one-photon (97.7–95.2 nm) or three-photon (292.9–285.6 nm) resonances, and a one-color 3+1 scheme via 3s falls 4,000 cm⁻¹ short of the 140,525 cm⁻¹ limit, so it needs 3+2 or a second color. Listed for reference.',
        S: '4p ³P at 308–311 nm (seven J″→J′ components), 4p ⁵P spin-forbidden; 4s ⁵S°/³S° are the one-photon resonances.',
        Cl: '4p ²D°₃/₂ at 235.33 nm from ²P°₃/₂; the same level is reached from the spin-orbit excited Cl*(²P°₁/₂) at 237.79 nm, which lets one laser scan both.',
        Br: 'ASD labels the 5p levels in jK coupling, e.g. 4p⁴(³P₂)5p ²[1]°₃/₂ (the “⁴D°₃/₂” of LS-coupling papers) at 260.6 nm.',
        I: '6p ²[3]°₅/₂ at 304.67 nm from ²P°₃/₂; 6p′ ²[2]°₃/₂ at 306.73 nm from I*(²P°₁/₂). Spin-orbit splitting 7603 cm⁻¹.',
